// Quick Sort



1. Quicksort’s partition step behaves like a two-pointer technique, where:
        You take a target (pivot)
2. Rearrange elements such that:
        All elements ≤ pivot → left side
3. All elements > pivot → right side
4. Order inside each side does NOT matter

+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++

6. The chosen element ( pivot ) always gets to its best possible solution due to last swap

